      "text": "You won't believe how big Alaska really is. Most people know Texas is huge, but Alaska makes it look surprisingly small. Alaska is the largest state in the United States, covering about 665,000 square miles. Now, here's where things get crazy. Alaska is actually bigger than Texas, California, and Montana combined. Imagine placing all three states together on a map. Alaska would still be larger. And here's another incredible fact. Alaska has more coastline than any other US state. Did you think Alaska was this big?",
